FIGURE's patch 5 of 5 to ImPlot3D (commit c54525f8d46cece384cc2618761a2c55016b06db, the submodule of cimplot3d v0.5).

A right click on a 3-D plot's legend opened no menu (#15, finding U7): HandleInput opens the menus from a right click
the plot's button holds, and over the legend the legend's own button (ButtonBehavior in RenderLegend, after the
plot's, with AllowOverlap) takes the pointer, so the plot is neither hovered nor held there; the "##LegendContext"
branch of the menus could only open from the plot's menu. A right button released over the legend (hovered on the
frame before, as the legend is drawn after the input), with no rotation drag and the plot's menus on, now opens the
legend's menu, as ImPlot's legend does. Applied to third_party/implot3d/implot3d.cpp; without it
src/tests/fortran/figure_test_plot_frame_3d_menus.F90's case 3 finds no "H" to click on the current path. To offer
upstream.

--- a/implot3d.cpp
+++ b/implot3d.cpp
@@ -2853,6 +2853,11 @@
         plot.ContextClick = false;
         plot.OpenContextThisFrame = true;
     }
+    // FIGURE: a right click released on the legend opens the legend's menu, as ImPlot's does: the legend's button takes
+    // the pointer from the plot's there (plot.Hovered and plot.Held stay false), so the click above never comes
+    if (plot.Items.Legend.Hovered && ImGui::IsMouseReleased(ImGuiMouseButton_Right) && !rotating &&
+        !ImHasFlag(plot.Flags, ImPlot3DFlags_NoMenus))
+        plot.OpenContextThisFrame = true;
 
     if (plot.OpenContextThisFrame) {
         if (plot.Items.Legend.Hovered)
